This is retained as an explicit diagnostic and is NOT removed from primary evaluation.

Reason:

the dedicated repair lifecycle fixture proves the Task-2 corruption path exactly:

RAW
-> SENSED
-> PROCESSED_A
-> PROCESSED_B
-> AT_EGRESS
-> REPAIR_PENDING
-> AT_EGRESS
-> VERIFIED
-> DONE

with immutable provenance and correct recomputation.

The loaded-world misses are caused by the inherited 32-epoch service envelope:

some corrupted requests first reach egress at age 30-31,
leaving insufficient epochs for detect -> repair -> mandatory reverify
before expiry.

This is the same class of benchmark boundary established by the accepted
Task-1G / post-Task1G service-envelope lineage.

R3 does NOT change:

expiry;
scheduler;
load;
